# L §5.14.3: flows(m[keys], span) — "On a day a statement covers, the observations that fulfil the move's instances
# stand in for them (§5.19)."  st_01 covers konto in 2026-01 and its row r1 fulfils rent[2026-01] at 2 850.00 PLN
# (planned 2 800.00): flows(rent, 2026-01) is 2 850.00 PLN; February, not covered, counts the plan, 2 800.00 PLN.
# (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.14.3: flows over a modelled-past instance.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-15
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input bank: observed
input rent_amt: money PLN
input rent_dom: int

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
place landlord: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move rent[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, rent_dom)
  leg cash from konto to landlord amount rent_amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  rent_amt = 2 800.00 PLN
  rent_dom = 3
  opening[konto] = 10 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

version st_01
  cite s
  governs 2026-01
  known 2026-02-02
  covers konto
  anchor konto
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-01-03, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to landlord amount 2 850.00 PLN, fulfils: rent[2026-01])

ask q: flows(rent, 2026-01), flows(rent, 2026-02)
=== expect
q: (2 850.00 PLN, 2 800.00 PLN)
...
